This is the end of the video. Thank you for watching until the end.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.530
You're going to say something annoying, aren't you?

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:11.310
Then, let's get rid of Koubi!

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:13.430
Oh, that's a good idea!

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:18.240
These two are the 3AA Dragon.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.680
That's right! They're Lovely Angels!

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:21.720
Oh, sorry.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.100
Hey, focus on the fight.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.300
Are they the 3AA Dragon?

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:27.450
Lovely Angels!

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.550
Hey, it's a dirty pair. If you get in, it's really a dirty pair.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.210
I can hear you!

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:38.390
Excuse me.

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:42.920
We have an urgent request. Please stop Brian's rampage with the power of the two of you.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:46.320
All right. Will you take us to the computer room?

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:52.670
Yes. The computer room is locked by Brian, but if we get close to it, we can somehow...

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:17.920
Don't call me an angel.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:20.340
Because to take the bone and the contact...

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.520
Mugi!

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:22.150
That's right!

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:31.230
Listen to me!

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:34.030
You're going to get on the capsule on your own!

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:36.990
And you're going to bring our ship with you, Nanmo!

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:40.490
The transmitter in the room is broken, so I can't get in touch from here.

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.450
You're the only one who can do it, right?

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:43.150
Got it?

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:47.870
Now, get caught!

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:48.860
Uncle!

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:50.430
My favorite cat!

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:00.500
Are you okay?

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:02.060
Trust your cute pet.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.480
Don't fall

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.140
Then let go

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.970
Are you kidding me?

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:20.840
It's hot, don't cut it out

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:21.380
Right?

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.930
Are you kidding me?

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.300
I'm working on something important so don't complain about it!

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:09.850
Complaining complaining...

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.010
Don't complain about me!

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:12.610
Complaining complaining...

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:13.240
I'm moving!

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:14.930
Hang in there!

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.890
It's not the exhaust duct of the incinerator!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:02.820
Correct!

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:04.030
Eeeeh!?

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:05.600
If I just stick it in like this, it'll burn!

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:08.450
Don't you know that the incinerator system here sparks every 5 seconds?

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:12.390
It's safe if you turn it around in the meantime!

00:15:12.710 --> 00:15:14.430
Who's in charge of the incinerator system?

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:16.400
Ah! Brian!

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:18.690
I knew it! I didn't think about it!

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:20.360
This is bad!

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:43.160
I'm going to act without thinking about anything else!

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:44.950
Then, Kanshi!

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.670
Don't mess around and go quickly!

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:48.730
Come on, come on, hurry up!

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:50.730
Don't push me so much!

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.940
I think I was saved thanks to you!

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:55.660
If you weren't there, this wouldn't have happened!

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:26.090
I'm going to take a picture of it.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.330
What? You are different from humans.

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:37.170
Rather, you are closer to me.

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:40.760
What is the cause of this nonsense, Brian?

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:42.960
The cause is you guys.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:46.330
Humans betrayed me.

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:47.920
You are the one who betrayed me, right?

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:50.220
I am in charge of all the systems in the tower.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:55.820
But there was a unit that I didn't know existed in the tower.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.030
As I thought, it was Zeebo.

00:16:57.630 --> 00:16:59.970
When that unit was activated, I...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.840
I learned that I lost a lot of memories.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:04.100
Then I'll let you get rid of it.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:05.200
So if you say yes,

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:07.900
The unit has already been cleared.

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:09.790
I won't quit.

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:13.250
Brian was a low-pitched mobile type computer, wasn't he?

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:13.850
That's right.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:15.340
Nanmo, start the thermo sensor.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:16.160
Yes.

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:17.490
Set to the lowest level.

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:20.270
The main laser is count 15.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.670
Are you serious?

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.640
Hey, Brian, you heard it, didn't you?

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:26.670
If you don't want to be destroyed,

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:28.730
Be a good boy right away.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:29.070
Thank you for watching!

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:31.140
The laser is different from the one you have.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:32.940
Neratin!

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:34.780
Oh, you're so cute!

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:35.580
Namo!

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:29.850
Another one, D.D.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.420
The name of the chair is engraved on it, isn't it?

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:32.820
That's unnecessary!

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:40.150
You're smart, so there's something I'd like to ask you.

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:43.470
Of course you have the data of the two of us, right?

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:44.170
Yes.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:45.930
Then which do you prefer, me or Yuri?

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:47.210
No!

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:50.780
If you give me the answer, I won't bother you anymore.

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:51.890
That's meaningless.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:54.700
You can't give me the answer.

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:57.670
Idiot! Doji! The assembly of the Invincible Collapse Corridor!

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:01.320
I'm doing it.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:09.780
Be careful, it's your chance!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:10.260
Ja!

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:10.860
What?

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:14.780
Ask Brian for a break and get in touch with Warp Terminal!

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:38.240
What the hell are you trying to do?

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:49.690
It doesn't matter if it's garbage, gas, dust, or anything!

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:52.170
I'll be the one to control the warp coordinates!

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:55.840
Oh, there's a garbage line that's being disposed of for a good reason.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:58.880
It's the first time, so I don't know what's going to happen.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:01.490
Hurry up and do it!

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:02.740
Hey!

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:03.810
Is it okay?

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:15.980
As rumored, Dirty Pair.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.240
Planet Lamell's destruction incident.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:20.520
3,521 injured.

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:27.180
The computer will be a mess if one of the parts gets into it, right?

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:28.340
What happens if it falls to the space ship?

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:31.370
But there's nothing we can do about it!

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:35.820
This is Warp Terminal. We've confirmed the warp coordinates.

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:39.850
Uh, uh, are you sure this is the right place?

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:42.770
What's your name and check number?

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:45.750
If you keep talking nonsense, I'll put it on the 3WA's blacklist!

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:48.140
Ah! Warp preparation, hurry!

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:52.600
Huh? What? What are you plotting?

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:58.710
I don't trust you guys. I won't forgive humans.

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:02.100
Dirty PA, restore communication!

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:05.720
Warp 10 seconds!

00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:06.640
9...

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:07.880
8...

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:08.640
7...

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:11.690
Something I don't know must happen.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:14.070
Warp!

00:21:35.530 --> 00:21:38.740
What the hell have you guys been up to all night?

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:42.100
Hey, are you listening?

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:43.900
Kei! Yuri!

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:46.910
Get out of the way!

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:49.830
Hey, Kei, let's go together.

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:53.760
I'm going to bed now.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:55.960
What is this?

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:58.160
I have to make a computer again.

00:21:58.160 --> 00:21:58.380
I have to fix it.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:00.920
You did a good job.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:02.660
I'm glad you said Dirty Pairs.

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:12.030
But I wonder if Brian's answer came out.

00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:13.550
It's obvious.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:15.440
I'm one

00:24:03.800 --> 00:24:04.280
And that's it!

00:24:04.280 --> 00:24:06.600
That's it?

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:07.780
Yeah, yeah!

00:24:10.750 --> 00:24:11.070
Hey!

00:24:11.270 --> 00:24:12.300
Come on, come on!

00:24:12.320 --> 00:24:13.860
Yuuri-san, translate it and give it to me!

00:24:13.940 --> 00:24:14.140
Okay!

00:24:14.850 --> 00:24:17.900
Next time on Kawaii Tenshu wa Munage ga Osuki!

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:19.040
You don't have to overdo it!

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:20.340
I don't get it!

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:22.520
Interesting!
